 "assumptions": [
  "Each team gets one question per person per day, asked at a random minute while the asker is awake.",
  "An awake person sees a message and answers within 15 minutes. A sleeping person answers 15 minutes after waking. Nobody is counted as woken up early, so a night ping never speeds up an answer.",
  "Group chat: every member gets a notification, and the person who knows always sees the question and answers. Both are generous to the group chat.",
  "Best guess: the asker messages the part's owner from the team plan. If someone else changed it recently, the owner always knows who and says so, and the asker passes the question on at their next waking minute. Owners asking about their own part check git and message whoever changed it. For parts with no owner in the plan, or answers nobody can point to, the asker falls back to the group chat.",
  "WhoKnows: the real agents run on every question. They ask who knows, then search the shareable notes of those people, then everyone's. If no quote contains the answer, the agent hands the question to the best match, then the next one if the first says not me, with the same 15 minute rule. After two misses the asker falls back to the group chat and pays its full cost, night pings included.",
  "About a quarter of answers belong to someone who changed a part recently rather than its owner, and a few belong to someone who left no trace in the plan, CODEOWNERS, git, or their agent. Half of all answers are written in notes their holder shares, 15% sit in drafts that need an OK, and the rest are only in someone's head. The second table varies the written share."
 ],
